      "dcterms:title": "Planscherel Measure on Eq(2)",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Ahmedov1, H.",
        "Duru2, I. H.",
        "1"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20211127",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9808030",
      "dcterms:abstract": "Following the construction of the invariant integral and the scalar product for the quantum Euclidean group Eq(2), we obtained the full matrix elements of its unitary irreducible representations from SUq(2) by contraction and then derived the Planscherel measure. July 1998 1E–mail : hagi@fge1.gursey.gov.tr and duru@fge1.gursey.gov.tr 1",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-math-9808030v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-math-9808030v1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-2311.05446v3",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "New Brunn--Minkowski and functional inequalities via convexity of entropy",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "AISHWARYA, GAUTAM",
        "ROTEM, LIRAN"
      ],
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.05446",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We study the connection between the concavity properties of a measure ν and the convexity properties of the associated relative entropy D(·∥ν) along optimal transport. As a corollary we prove a new dimensional Brunn–Minkowski inequality for centered star-shaped bod- ies, when the measure ν is log-concave with a p-homogeneous potential (such as the Gaussian measure). Our method allows us to go beyond the usual convexity assumption on the sets that is fundamentally essential for the standard differential-geometric technique in this area. We then take a finer look at the convexity properties of the Gauss- ian relative entropy, which yields new functional inequalities. First we obtain curvature and dimensional reinforcements to Otto–Villani’s HWI inequality in Gauss space, when restricted to even strongly log-concave measures. As corollaries, we obtain improved versions of Gross’ Loga- rithmic Sobolev inequality and Talagrand’s transportation cost inequal- ity in this setting.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-2311.05446v3/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-2311.05446v3"
    },
    {
