      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "2023",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.05446"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/aiston-morton-1997",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Idempotents of Hecke algebras of type A",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Aiston, A. K.",
        "Morton, H. R."
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "1997",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9702017"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-q-alg-9702017v2",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Idempotents of Hecke algebras of type A",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Aiston, A.K.",
        "∗, H.R. Morton"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20190207",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9702017",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We use a skein-theoretic version of the Hecke algebras of type A to present three-dimensional diagrammatic views of Gyoja’s idempotent el- ements, based closely on the corresponding Young diagram λ. In this context we give straightforward calculations for the eigenvalues fλ and mλ of two natural central elements in the Hecke algebras, namely the full curl and the sum of the Murphy operators. We discuss their calculation also in terms of the framing factor associated to the appropriate irreducible representation of the quantum group, SU(N)q.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-q-alg-9702017v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-q-alg-9702017v2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/aitken1956",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:Book"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Determinants and Matrices",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Aitken, A. C."
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "1956"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-hep-th-9609174v2",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "arXiv:hep-th/9609174v2 23 Sep 1996",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Akemann∗, G.",
        "Damgaard†, P. H.",
        "Magnea‡, U.",
        "Nishigaki§, S."
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20241126",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9609174",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We prove the universality of correlation functions of chiral unitary and unitary ensembles of ran- dom matrices in the microscopic limit. The essence of the proof consists in reducing the three-term recursion relation for the relevant orthogonal polynomials into a Bessel equation governing the local asymptotics around the origin. The possible physical interpretation as the universality of soft spectrum of the Dirac operator is brieﬂy discussed. PACS: 05.45.+b, 11.15.Pg, 11.30.Rd e-mail addresses: ∗akemann@itp.uni-hannover.de, † phdamg, ‡ umagnea, § shinsuke@alf.nbi.dk",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-hep-th-9609174v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-hep-th-9609174v2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-1108.3035v2",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Random Matrix Theory for the Hermitian Wilson Dirac Operator and the chGUE – GUE Transition",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Akemann1, Gernot",
        "Nagao2, Taro"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20220430",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1108.3035",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We introduce a random two-matrix model interpolating between a chiral Hermitian (2n + ν) × (2n+ν) matrix and a second Hermitian matrix without symmetries. These are taken from the chiral Gaussian Unitary Ensemble (chGUE) and Gaussian Unitary Ensemble (GUE), respectively. In the microscopic large-n limit in the vicinity of the chGUE (which we denote by weakly non-chiral limit) this theory is in one to one correspondence to the partition function of Wilson chiral perturbation theory in the epsilon regime, such as the related two matrix-model previously introduced in [20, 21]. For a generic number of ﬂavours and rectangular block matrices in the chGUE part we derive an eigenvalue representation for the partition function displaying a Pfaﬃan structure. In the quenched case with ν = 0, 1 we derive all spectral correlations functions in our model for ﬁnite-n, given in terms of skew-orthogonal polynomials. The latter are expressed as Gaussian integrals over standard Laguerre polynomials. In the weakly non-chiral microscopic limit this yields all corresponding quenched eigenvalue correlation functions of the Hermitian Wilson operator.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-1108.3035v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-1108.3035v2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-1908.07065v3",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Non-perturbative approaches to the quantum Seiberg–Witten curve",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Alba Grassia, Jie Gub",
        "Mariñob, Marcos"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20200721",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.07065",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We study various non-perturbative approaches to the quantization of the Seiberg– Witten curve of N = 2, SU(2) super Yang–Mills theory, which is closely related to the modiﬁed Mathieu operator. The ﬁrst approach is based on the quantum WKB periods and their resurgent properties. We show that these properties are encoded in the TBA equations of Gaiotto–Moore– Neitzke determined by the BPS spectrum of the theory, and we relate the Borel-resummed quantum periods to instanton calculus. In addition, we use the TS/ST correspondence to obtain a closed formula for the Fredholm determinant of the modiﬁed Mathieu operator. Finally, by using blowup equations, we explain the connection between this operator and the τ function of Painlev´e III. arXiv:1908.07065v3 [hep-th] 20 Jul 2020",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-1908.07065v3/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-1908.07065v3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/albuquerque-majid1999",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Quasialgebra structure of the octonions",
      "dcterms:creator": [
