    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-2004.04939v1",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "BRAID GROUP ACTION ON THE MODULE CATEGORY OF",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "ALGEBRAS, QUANTUM AFFINE"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20200412",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.04939",
      "dcterms:abstract": "Let g0 be a simple Lie algebra of type ADE and let U ′ q(g) be the corre- sponding untwisted quantum aﬃne algebra. We show that there exists an action of the braid group B(g0) on the quantum Grothendieck ring Kt(g) of Hernandez-Leclerc’s category C 0 g . Focused on the case of type AN−1, we construct a family of monoidal autofunctors {Si}i∈Z on a localization TN of the category of ﬁnite-dimensional graded modules over the quiver Hecke algebra of type A∞. Under an isomorphism between the Grothendieck ring K(TN) of TN and the quantum Grothendieck ring Kt(A(1) N−1), the functors {Si}1≤i≤N−1 recover the action of the braid group B(AN−1). We inves- tigate further properties of these functors.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-2004.04939v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-2004.04939v1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-1304.0323v3",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "SYMMETRIC QUIVER HECKE ALGEBRAS",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "ALGEBRAS, R-MATRICES OF QUANTUM AFFINE"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20210328",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.0323",
      "dcterms:abstract": "Let J be a set of pairs consisting of good U ′ q(g)-modules and invertible elements in the base ﬁeld C(q). The distribution of poles of normalized R-matrices yields Khovanov-Lauda-Rouquier algebras RJ (β) for each β∈ Q+. We deﬁne a func- torFβ from the category of graded RJ (β)-modules to the category of U ′ q(g)-modules. The functorF = ⨁ β ∈Q+Fβ sends convolution products of ﬁnite-dimensional graded RJ (β)-modules to tensor products of ﬁnite-dimensional U ′ q(g)-modules. It is exact if RJ is of ﬁnite type A, D, E. If V (̟1) is the fundamental representation of U ′ q(ˆslN ) of weight ̟1 and J = {( V (̟1), q2i) | i∈ Z } , then RJ is the Khovanov-Lauda-Rouquier algebra of type A∞. The corresponding functor F sends a ﬁnite-dimensional graded RJ -module to a module in CJ , where CJ is the category of ﬁnite-dimensional inte- grable U ′ q(ˆslN )-modules M such that every composition factor of M appears as a composition factor of a tensor product of modules of the form V (̟1)q2s (s∈ Z). Focusing on this case, we obtain an abelian rigid graded tensor categ oryTJ by local- izing the category of ﬁnite-dimensional graded RJ -modules. The functor F factors throughTJ . Moreover, the Grothendieck ring of the category CJ is isomorphic to the Grothendieck ring of TJ at q = 1.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-1304.0323v3/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-1304.0323v3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-1304.2705v1",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "FROM STATE INTEGRALS TO q-SERIES",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "ALIDIS, STA VROS GAROUF",
        "KASHAEV, RINAT"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20180918",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.2705",
      "dcterms:abstract": "It is well-known to the experts that multi-dimensional state integra ls of prod- ucts of Faddeev’s quantum dilogarithm which arise in Quantum Topolog y can be written as ﬁnite sums of products of basic hypergeometric series in q = e2πiτ and ˜q = e− 2πi/τ . We illustrate this fact by giving a detailed proof for a family of one-dimens ional integrals which includes state-integral invariants of 4 1 and 5 2 knots.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-1304.2705v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-1304.2705v1"
    },
