    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-hep-th-9310070v1",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Quantum dilogarithm",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Faddeev1, L.D.",
        "2",
        "†",
        "Kashaev1, R.M.",
        "∗",
        "†"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20241126",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9310070",
      "dcterms:abstract": "A quantum generalization of Rogers’ ﬁve term, or “pentagon” dilogarithm identity is suggested. It is shown that the classical limit gives usual Rogers’ identity. The case where the quantum identity is realized in ﬁnite dimensional space is also considered and the quantum dilogarithm is constructed as a function on Fermat curve, while the identity itself is equivalent to the restricted star-triangle relation introduced by Bazhanov and Baxter. † Supported by the Russian Academy of Sciences and Academy of Finland ∗On leave of absence from St. Petersburg Nuclear Physics Institute, Gatchina, St. Petersburg 188350, Russia",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-hep-th-9310070v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-hep-th-9310070v1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-2012.12159v3",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "A FUNK PERSPECTIVE ON BILLIARDS, PROJECTIVE GEOMETRY AND MAHLER VOLUME",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "FAIFMAN, DMITRY"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20210423",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.12159",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We explore connections furnished by the Funk metric, a relative of the Hilbert metric, between projective geometry, billiards, convex geome- try and aﬃne inequalities. We ﬁrst show that many metric invariants of the Funk metric are invariant under projective maps, as well as under projective duality. These include the Holmes-Thompson volume and surface area of con- vex subsets, and the length spectrum of their boundary, extending results of Holmes-Thompson and ´Alvarez Paiva on Sch¨aﬀer’s dual girth conjecture. We explore in particular Funk billiards, which generalize hyperbolic billiards in the same way that Minkowski billiards generalize Euclidean ones, and extend a result of Gutkin-Tabachnikov on the duality of Minkowski billiards. We next consider the volume of outward balls in Funk geometry. We con- jecture a general aﬃne inequality corresponding to the volume maximizers, which includes the Blaschke-Santal´o and centro-aﬃne isoperimetric inequali- ties as limit cases, and prove it for unconditional bodies, yielding a new proof of the volume entropy conjecture for the Hilbert metric for unconditional bodies. As a by-product, we obtain generalizations to higher moments of inequalities of Ball and Huang-Li, which in turn strengthen the Blaschke-Santal´o inequal- ity for unconditional bodies. Lastly, we introduce a regularization of the total volume of a smooth strictly convex 2-dimensional set equipped with the Funk metric, resembling the O’Hara M¨obius energy of a knot, and show that it is a projective invariant of the convex body.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-2012.12159v3/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-2012.12159v3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-1412.4711v1",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "CHARACTER VARIETIES FOR SL(3, C): THE FIGURE EIGHT KNOT",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "FALBEL, E.",
        "GUILLOUX, A.",
        "KOSELEFF, P.-V."
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20141216",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1412.4711",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We give a description of several representation varieties of the fundamental group of the complement of the ﬁgure eight knot in PGL(3, C) or PSL(3, C). We obtain a description of the projection of the representation variety into the character variety of the boundary torus into SL(3, C).",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-1412.4711v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-1412.4711v1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-2410.20973v1",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "SUMMABILITY FOR STATE INTEGRALS OF HYPERBOLIC KNOTS",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "FANTINI, VERONICA",
        "WHEELER, CAMPBELL"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20241028",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.20973",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We prove conjectures of Garoufalidis-Gu-Mari˜no [9] that perturbative series associated with the hyperbolic knots 41 and 52 are resurgent and Borel summable. In the process, we give an algorithm that can be used to explicitly compute the Borel–Laplace resummation as a combination of state integrals of Andersen–Kashaev [1]. This gives a complete description of the resurgent structure in these examples and allows for explicit computations of Stokes constants.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-2410.20973v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-2410.20973v1"
    },
