    {
      "@id": "references/francaviglia2003",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:Article"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Hyperbolic volume of representations of fundamental groups of cusped 3-manifolds",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Francaviglia, Stefano"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "2003",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0305275"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-math-0305275v1",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Hyperbolic volume of representations of fundamental groups of cusped 3-manifolds",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Francaviglia12, Stefano"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20210917",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0305275",
      "dcterms:abstract": "Let W be a compact manifold and let ρ be a representation of its fundamental group into PSL(2, C). Then the volume of ρ is deﬁned by taking any ρ-equivariant map from the universal cover f W to H3 and then by integrating the pull-back of the hyperbolic volume form on a fundamental domain. It turns out that such a volume does not depend on the choice of the equivariant map. Dunﬁeld extended this construction to the case of a non-compact (cusped) manifold M, but he did not prove the volume is well-deﬁned in all cases. We prove here that the volume of a representation is always well- deﬁned and depends only on the representation. Moreover, we show that this volume can be easily computed by straightening any ideal triangulation of M. We show that the volume of a representation is bounded from above by the relative simplicial volume of M. Finally, we prove a rigidity theorem for representations of the fundamental group of a hyperbolic manifold. Namely, we prove that if M is hyperbolic and vol(ρ) = vol(M) then ρ is discrete and faithful.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-math-0305275v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-math-0305275v1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-math-9909088v1",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "The Gauss Map and a Noncompact Riemann-Roch Formula for Constructible Sheaves on Semiabelian Varieties",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Franecki, J.",
        "Kapranov, M."
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20180820",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9909088",
      "dcterms:abstract": "For an irreducible subvariety Z in an algebraic group G we deﬁne an integer gdeg(Z) ≥0 as the degree, in a certain sense, of the Gauss map of Z. It can be regarded as a substitution for the intersection index of the conormal bundle to Z with the zero section of T ∗G, even though G may not be compact. For G a semiabelian variety (in particular, an algebraic torus (C∗)n), we prove a Riemann- Roch type formula for constructible sheaves on G which involves our substitutions for the intersection indicies. As a corollary, we get that a perverse sheaf on such a G has nonnegative Euler characteristic, generalizing a theorem of Loeser-Sabbah.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-math-9909088v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-math-9909088v1"
    },
