    {
      "@id": "references/angled-survey",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "From angled triangulations to hyperbolic structures",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Futer, David",
        "Guéritaud, Fran¸cois"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20190704",
      "bibo:doi": "10.1090/conm/541/10683",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://doi.org/10.1090/conm/541/10683",
      "dcterms:abstract": "This survey paper contains an elementary exposition of Casson and Rivin’s technique for ﬁnding the hyperbolic metric on a 3–manifold M with toroidal boundary. We also survey a number of applications of this technique. The method involves subdividing M into ideal tetrahedra and solving a system of gluing equations to ﬁnd hyperbolic shapes for the tetrahedra. The gluing equations decompose into a linear and non-linear part. The solutions to the linear equations form a convex polytope A. The solution to the non-linear part (unique if it exists) is a critical point of a certain volume functional on this polytope. The main contribution of this paper is an elementary proof of Rivin’s theorem that a critical point of the volume functional on A produces a complete hyperbolic structure on M.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/angled-survey/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/angled-survey"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/futer-gueritaud-angled",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:Chapter"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "From angled triangulations to hyperbolic structures",
      "dcterms:creator": [
