        "Guéritaud, François"
      ],
      "dcterms:isPartOf": "Contemporary Mathematics"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-1204.4824v2",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Spectral networks",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Gaiotto, Davide",
        "Moore2, 1 Gregory W.",
        "Neitzke3, Andrew"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20131008",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1204.4824",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We introduce new geometric objects called spectral networks. Spectral net- works are networks of trajectories on Riemann surfaces obeying certain local rules. Spec- tral networks arise naturally in four-dimensional N = 2 theories coupled to surface defects, particularly the theories of class S. In these theories spectral networks provide a useful tool for the computation of BPS degeneracies: the network directly determines the degen- eracies of solitons living on the surface defect, which in turn determine the degeneracies for particles living in the 4d bulk. Spectral networks also lead to a new map between ﬂat GL(K, C) connections on a two-dimensional surface C and ﬂat abelian connections on an appropriate branched cover Σ of C. This construction produces natural coordinate sys- tems on moduli spaces of ﬂat GL(K, C) connections on C, which we conjecture are cluster coordinate systems. arXiv:1204.4824v2 [hep-th] 6 Oct 2013",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-1204.4824v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-1204.4824v2"
    },
