    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-1808.08110v1",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Exceptional quantum geometry and particle physics II",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "II, AND PARTICLE PHYSICS"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20180826",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.08110",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We continue the study undertaken in [13] of the relevance of the exceptional Jordan algebra J8 3 of hermitian 3 × 3 octonionic matrices for the description of the internal space of the fundamental fermions of the Standard Model with 3 generations. By using the suggestion of [30] (properly justiﬁed here) that the Jordan algebra J8 2 of hermitian 2× 2 octonionic matrices is relevant for the description of the internal space of the fundamental fermions of one generation, we show that, based on the same principles and the same framework as in [13], there is a way to describe the internal space of the 3 generations which avoids the introduction of new fundamental fermions and where there is no problem with respect to the electroweak symmetry. LPT-ORSAY 18-78 1Laboratoire de Physique Th´eorique, CNRS, Universit´e Paris-Sud, Universit´e Paris- Saclay, Bˆatiment 210, F-91 405 Orsay. Michel.Dubois-Violette@u-psud.fr 2INRNE, Bulgarian Academy of Sciences, Tsarigradsko Chaussee 72, BG-1784 Soﬁa. ivbortodorov@gmail.com",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-1808.08110v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-1808.08110v1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-1501.04614v1",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "KNOT CABLING AND THE DEGREE OF THE COLORED JONES",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "II, POLYNOMIAL"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20211110",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1501.04614",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We continue our study of the degree of the colored Jones polynomial under knot cabling started in [8]. Under certain hypothesis on this degree, we determine how the Jones slopes and the linear term behave under cabling. As an application we verify Garoufalidis’ Slope Conjecture and a conjecture of [8] for cables of a two-parameter family of closed 3-braids called 2-fusion knots.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-1501.04614v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-1501.04614v1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-2205.07095v1",
      "@type": [
