    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-2412.02281v1",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Explicit evaluation of the q -Stokes matrices for certain conﬂuent hypergeometric q -diﬀerence equations",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Jinghong Lin, Yiming Ma",
        "Xu, Xiaomeng"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20241203",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.02281",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We prove a connection formula for the basic hypergeomtric function nϕn−1 (a1, ..., an−1, 0; b1, ..., bn−1; q, z) by using the q-Borel resummation. As an application, we compute q-Stokes matrices of a special conﬂuent hypergeometric q-diﬀerence system with an irregular singularity. We show that by letting q →1, the q-Stokes matrices recover the known expressions of the Stokes matrices of the corresponding conﬂuent hypergeometric diﬀerential system.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-2412.02281v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-2412.02281v1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-math-9810105v2",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "arXiv:math/9810105v2 [math.CO] 26 Mar 1999",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "JINHO BAIK, PERCY DEIFT",
        "JOHANSSON, KURT"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20241126",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9810105",
      "dcterms:abstract": "The authors consider the length, lN, of the length of the longest increasing subsequence of a random permutation of N numbers. The main result in this paper is a proof that the distribution function for lN, suitably centered and scaled, converges to the Tracy-Widom distribution [TW1] of the largest eigenvalue of a random GUE matrix. The authors also prove con- vergence of moments. The proof is based on the steepest decent method for Riemann-Hilbert problems, introduced by Deift and Zhou in 1993 [DZ1] in the context of integrable systems. The applicability of the Riemann-Hilbert technique depends, in turn, on the determinantal formula of Gessel [Ge] for the Poissonization of the distribution function of lN.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-math-9810105v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-math-9810105v2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-math-9906120v3",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Discrete orthogonal polynomial ensembles and the Plancherel measure",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Johansson, By Kurt"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20180907",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9906120",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We consider discrete orthogonal polynomial ensembles which are discrete analogues of the orthogonal polynomial ensembles in random matrix theory. These ensembles occur in certain problems in combinatorial probability and can be thought of as probability measures on partitions. The Meixner ensemble is related to a two-dimensional directed growth model, and the Charlier ensemble is related to the lengths of weakly increasing subsequences in random words. The Krawtchouk ensemble occurs in connection with zig-zag paths in random domino tilings of the Aztec diamond, and also in a certain simpliﬁed directed ﬁrst-passage percolation model. We use the Charlier ensemble to investigate the asymptotics of weakly increasing subsequences in random words and to prove a conjecture of Tracy and Widom. As a limit of the Meixner ensemble or the Charlier ensemble we obtain the Plancherel measure on partitions, and using this we prove a conjecture of Baik, Deift and Johansson that under the Plancherel measure, the distribution of the lengths of the ﬁrst k rows in the partition, appropriately scaled, converges to the asymptotic joint distribution for the k largest eigenvalues of a random matrix from the Gaussian Unitary Ensemble. In this problem a certain discrete kernel, which we call the discrete Bessel kernel, plays an important role.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-math-9906120v3/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-math-9906120v3"
    },
