    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-2404.19155v2",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "Octahedral coordinates from the Wirtinger presentation",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "McPhail-Snyder, Calvin"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20250516",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.19155",
      "dcterms:abstract": "Let ρ be a representation of a knot group (or more generally, the funda- mental group of a tangle complement) into SL2(C) expressed in terms of the Wirtinger generators of a diagram D. This diagram also determines an ideal triangulation of the complement called the octahedral decompo- sition. ρ induces a hyperbolic structure on the complement of D, and in this note we give a direct algebraic formula for the geometric parameters of the octahedral decomposition induced by this structure. Our formula gives a new, explicit criterion for whether ρ occurs as a critical point of the diagram’s Neumann-Zagier–Yokota potential function.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-2404.19155v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-2404.19155v2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-2601.05136v2",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "State integrals for the quantized SL 2 ( C ) Chern-Simons invariant",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "McPhail-Snyder, Calvin"
      ],
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.05136",
      "dcterms:abstract": "Previous work of the author and N. Reshetikhin deﬁnes an invariant Zψ N(K, ρ, µ) of a knot K, a representation ρ: π1(S3 \\ K) →SL2(C), and a logarithm µ of a meridian eigenvalue of ρ. It can be interpreted as a geometric twist of the Kashaev invariant or as a quantization of the SL2(C) Chern-Simons invariant and is deﬁned via a discrete state-sum involving quantum dilogarithms. In this paper we show how to express Zψ N(K, ρ, µ) as a sum over contour integrals in a space parametrizing hyperbolic struc- tures on the knot complement. Such state integral presentations are an important step in determining the asymptotics of quantum invariants as predicted by the Volume Conjecture. We discuss this perspective and the remaining obstacles to establishing exponential growth of Zψ N.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-2601.05136v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-2601.05136v2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "references/arxiv-2509.02354v2",
      "@type": [
        "fabio:Work",
        "bibo:AcademicArticle"
      ],
      "dcterms:title": "The holonomy braiding for U_xi(sl2) in terms of geometric quantum dilogarithms",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "MCPHAIL-SNYDER, CALVIN",
        "RESHETIKHIN, NICOLAI"
      ],
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.02354",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We derive an explicit formula for the holonomy R-matrix of quantum sl2 at a root of unity. We show it factorizes into a product of four quantum dilogarithms and satisfies a holonomy Yang-Baxter equation. This factorization extends previously known results and we collect many existing results needed for our computation.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-2509.02354v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-2509.02354v2"
    },
